# AI Dynamic Alternatives for Exceptions

## Goal Description
The goal is to dynamically generate suggested alternatives/resolutions using an LLM (Bedrock Converse/LangChain setup already available in the backend via [ai_router.py](file:///c:/Github%20Repo/Supply_chain/backend/routers/ai_router.py)) dynamically tailored to the context of a selected Supply Chain Exception. These alternatives will be stored in the database so they are only generated once per exception. A user can select an alternative, click "Use Alternative", and it will generate an actionable "Task" assigned in the database.

## Proposed Changes

### Database Changes
- Add a new table `exception_alternatives` with fields: `exception_id`, `alt_id`, `title`, `description`, `cost_impact`, `kpi_impact`, `tradeoff`.
- Add a new table `tasks` with fields: `task_id`, `exception_id`, `title`, `description`, `status`, `created_at`.

### Backend Changes ([anomaly_router.py](file:///c:/Github%20Repo/Supply_chain/backend/routers/anomaly_router.py) / [ai_router.py](file:///c:/Github%20Repo/Supply_chain/backend/routers/ai_router.py))
- **[MODIFY]** [backend/routers/anomaly_router.py](file:///c:/Github%20Repo/Supply_chain/backend/routers/anomaly_router.py)
  - Update `GET /api/anomaly/alternatives/{exception_id}` to:
    1. Query the `exception_alternatives` table for existing alternatives for `exception_id`.
    2. If found, return them.
    3. If not found, invoke the LLM via `ChatBedrockConverse` with the exception context to generate 3 options.
    4. Save the generated options to the `exception_alternatives` table and return them.
  - Update `POST /api/anomaly/approve` to explicitly create a record in the new `tasks` table and mark the exception as 'Investigating' or 'Mitigating'.

### Frontend Changes ([ExceptionsScreen.jsx](file:///c:/Github%20Repo/Supply_chain/frontend/src/components/ExceptionsScreen.jsx) & [ExceptionDashboard.jsx](file:///c:/Github%20Repo/Supply_chain/frontend/src/components/ExceptionDashboard.jsx))
- **[MODIFY]** [frontend/src/components/ExceptionsScreen.jsx](file:///c:/Github%20Repo/Supply_chain/frontend/src/components/ExceptionsScreen.jsx)
  - When an exception is selected, initiate a fetch to `GET /api/anomaly/alternatives/{exception_id}`.
  - Display a loading state while the LLM generates the initial alternatives.
  - Render the alternatives block below the exception details.
  - Add an "Authorize Selected Action" (Use Alternative) button.
  - Clicking this triggers `POST /api/anomaly/approve/{exception_id}` with the selected alternative ID to create the Task.

## Verification Plan
1. Send a GET request to `/api/anomaly/alternatives/EX-101` and verify the delay while the LLM generates.
2. Send the exact same GET request again and verify immediate response (DB cache hit).
3. Click "Use Alternative" on the UI and check the `tasks` SQLite table to ensure the new task row is inserted correctly.
